# Oracle GoldenGate (Interview Explanation)

What is Oracle GoldenGate?

> Oracle GoldenGate is Oracle's real-time data replication tool. It captures changes (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE) from a source database transaction log and replicates them to one or more target databases with very low latency.

Simple Example

Imagine you have:

* Oracle Database (Source)
* Oracle Database (Target)

Whenever a customer record is inserted into the source database, the same record should immediately appear in the target database.

Instead of copying the entire table every hour, GoldenGate replicates only the changed data almost instantly.

---

# Why Do We Need GoldenGate?

Suppose a company has:

* Production Database
* Reporting Database

Users keep inserting invoices into Production.

The Reporting database must always have the latest data.

Without GoldenGate:

    Production DB
             ↓
    Every Night
             ↓
    Reporting DB

Reports are one day old.

With GoldenGate:

    Production DB
             ↓
    Real-Time Replication
             ↓
    Reporting DB

Reports always show the latest data.

---

# GoldenGate Architecture

        Source Database
                │
        Transaction Logs (Redo Logs)
                │
        Extract Process
                │
        Trail Files
                │
        Data Pump
                │
        Network
                │
        Remote Trail Files
                │
        Replicat
                │
        Target Database
---

# Components

1. Extract Process
Reads database redo/transaction logs.

It captures:

    * INSERT
    * UPDATE
    * DELETE

It does not read the table directly.

Example:    INSERT INTO EMPLOYEE
            Extract captures this transaction.

---

2. Trail Files
    Extract writes the captured changes into Trail Files.
    Think of them as temporary files that store database changes.

---

3. Data Pump
    Transfers trail files from the source server to the target server.

    Benefits:

    * Reduces load on Extract
    * Supports remote replication
    * Better fault tolerance

---

4. Replicat
    Reads the trail files and applies the changes to the target database.

Example:

Source

    INSERT Employee
             ↓
        Replicat
             ↓
        Target

INSERT Employee

---

Complete Flow

    Application
        ↓
    Oracle Database
        ↓
    Redo Logs
        ↓
    Extract
        ↓
    Local Trail Files
        ↓
    Data Pump
        ↓
    Remote Trail Files
        ↓
    Replicat
        ↓
    Target Database

